    },
    {
      "speaker": "p2",
      "to": "p3",
      "stance": "opp",
      "cue": null,
      "quote": "                  Why don't you have a seat.",
      "block": 16
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p2",
      "to": "p3",
      "stance": "opp",
      "cue": null,
      "quote": "                  Enjoy the view.",
      "block": 17
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p4",
      "to": null,
      "stance": "neu",
      "cue": null,
      "quote": "Nexus designated Leon:  incept\n                  date April 10th, 2015 -- to be\n                  used in military experiments to\n                  determine how hyper metabolism\n                  functions in deep space.\n                  Nexus designated Batty incept\n                  data April 10th, 2015, combat\n                  model, level of self-sufficiency,\n                  optimum.",
      "block": 18
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p4",
      "to": null,
      "stance": "neu",
      "cue": null,
      "quote": "Here's something you might find\n                  interesting.  They have been built\n                  to emulate the human in every way\n                  except in its emotional spectrum.\n                  However, after a period of time\n                  it is only logical that such a\n                  'mechanism' would create its own\n                  emotional responses, hate, love,\n                  fear, anger, envy.",
      "block": 19
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p5",
      "to": "p4",
      "stance": "neu",
      "cue": null,
      "quote": "I know all that.",
      "block": 20
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p4",
      "to": "p5",
      "stance": "neu",
      "cue": null,
      "quote": "What about a summary then.",
      "block": 21
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p5",
      "to": "p4",
      "stance": "neu",
      "cue": null,
      "quote": "I think we're through for the night.",
      "block": 22
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p4",
      "to": "p5",
      "stance": "neu",
      "cue": null,
      "quote": "Mr. Deckard.",
      "block": 23
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p5",
      "to": "p4",
      "stance": "neu",
      "cue": null,
      "quote": "Yes?",
      "block": 24
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p4",
      "to": "p5",
      "stance": "neu",
      "cue": null,
      "quote": "Do you have something against\n                  science?",
      "block": 25
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p5",
      "to": "p4",
      "stance": "neu",
      "cue": null,
      "quote": "Not if it works.",
      "block": 26
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p4",
      "to": "p5",
      "stance": "neu",
      "cue": null,
      "quote": "And what in your estimation works?",
      "block": 27
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p5",
      "to": "p4",
      "stance": "neu",
      "cue": null,
      "quote": "The umbrella.",
      "block": 28
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p5",
      "to": null,
      "stance": "neu",
      "cue": null,
      "quote": "Every government that could was\n                  racing to populate their colonial\n                  territory.  But emigrants needed\n                  incentive.  Over-population and\n                  the greenhouse factor didn't seem\n                  to be enough; but owning a human\n                  look-a-like had lots of appeal.\n                  It was big industry, the competition\n                  was stiff and Tyrell was top of the\n                  line.",
      "block": 29
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p5",
      "to": null,
      "stance": "neu",
      "cue": null,
      "quote": "But so far they'd always managed\n                  to keep it quiet.  Not to say\n                  that once in a while there wasn't\n                  bad publicity.  Some fanatic\n                  bitching about equal rights for\n                  andies or an occasional trade union\n                  proclaiming it was aun-American for\n                  automatons to take jobs away from\n                  humans on the colony.",
      "block": 30
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p5",
      "to": null,
      "stance": "neu",
      "cue": null,
      "quote": "But what's more American than good\n                  old supply and demand?  The\n                  Government needed them, industry\n                  made them and the church backed\n                  them.  The big religious boys\n                  said that Androids, no matter how\n                  human, were objects; only God\n                  could make people. I'm not religious,\n                  but I was inclined to agree.\n                  Otherwise I'd be out of a job.",
      "block": 31
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p6",
      "to": "p5",
      "stance": "neu",
      "cue": null,
      "quote": "Hello, Mr. Deckard.  My name is\n                  Rachael.",
      "block": 32
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p6",
      "to": "p5",
      "stance": "neu",
      "cue": null,
      "quote": "It seems your department doesn't\n                  believe out new unit is to the\n                  public benefit.",
      "block": 33
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p5",
      "to": "p6",
      "stance": "neu",
      "cue": null,
      "quote": "A humanoid robot is like any other\n                  machine, it can be a benefit or a\n                  hazard.  If it's a benefit, it's\n                  not our problem.",
      "block": 34
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p6",
      "to": "p5",
      "stance": "neu",
      "cue": null,
      "quote": "But because your department can't\n                  do an adequate job in detecting\n                  the miniscule number at large,\n                  it's a problem.  Correct, Mr.\n                  Deckard?",
      "block": 35
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p6",
      "to": "p5",
      "stance": "neu",
      "cue": null,
      "quote": "You like our owl?",
      "block": 36
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p5",
      "to": "p6",
      "stance": "neu",
      "cue": null,
      "quote": "It's artificial?",
      "block": 37
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p6",
      "to": "p5",
      "stance": "neu",
      "cue": null,
      "quote": "Of course not.",
      "block": 38
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p6",
      "to": "p5",
      "stance": "neu",
      "cue": null,
      "quote": "You're in a very unique position,\n                  Mr. Deckard.  You could affect the\n                  future of this entire organization\n                  according to how you work your\n                  little test.",
      "block": 39
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p6",
      "to": "p5",
      "stance": "neu",
      "cue": null,
      "quote": "Are you apprehensive?",
      "block": 40
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p5",
      "to": "p6",
      "stance": "neu",
      "cue": null,
      "quote": "Why should I be?",
      "block": 41
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p6",
      "to": null,
      "stance": "neu",
      "cue": "RACHAEL",
      "quote": "Was that your dinner?",
      "block": 42
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p6",
      "to": null,
      "stance": "ally",
      "cue": "RACHAEL",
      "quote": "I'm sorry.  I called and found out\n                  you were on your way home.  These\n                  were already delivered to your\n                  department but I thought you\n                  should have copies as soon as\n                  possible.",
      "block": 43
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p6",
      "to": null,
      "stance": "ally",
      "cue": "RACHAEL",
      "quote": "I'm sorry.",
      "block": 44
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p6",
      "to": null,
      "stance": "ally",
      "cue": "RACHAEL",
      "quote": "It's the Nexus information you\n                  wanted.",
      "block": 45
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p5",
      "to": null,
      "stance": "ally",
      "cue": "DECKARD",
      "quote": "Thanks.",
      "block": 46
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p5",
      "to": null,
      "stance": "neu",
      "cue": "DECKARD",
      "quote": "Is there anything else?",
      "block": 47
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p6",
      "to": null,
      "stance": "ally",
      "cue": "RACHAEL",
      "quote": "I know you think it complicates\n                  your work, but I'm here to help.",
      "block": 48
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p5",
      "to": null,
      "stance": "opp",
      "cue": "DECKARD",
      "quote": "I've already got more help than\n                  I need.",
      "block": 49
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p6",
      "to": null,
      "stance": "ally",
      "cue": "RACHAEL",
      "quote": "I think you need more help than\n                  you've got.",
      "block": 50
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p6",
      "to": null,
      "stance": "neu",
      "cue": "RACHAEL",
      "quote": "There's two reasons a man rejects\n                  help.  Either because he's so good\n                  at what he does he doesn't think\n                  he needs it, or he's so insecure\n                  he can't admit it.",
      "block": 51
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p5",
      "to": null,
      "stance": "opp",
      "cue": "DECKARD",
      "quote": "Sounds like I'm an ass-hole either\n                  way, but the answer is still no.",
      "block": 52
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p6",
      "to": null,
      "stance": "ally",
      "cue": "RACHAEL",
      "quote": "Two of us might be more effective\n                  than one.",
      "block": 53
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p5",
      "to": null,
      "stance": "opp",
      "cue": "DECKARD",
      "quote": "I work alone.",
      "block": 54
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p6",
      "to": null,
      "stance": "opp",
      "cue": "RACHAEL",
      "quote": "No you don't.",
      "block": 55
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p6",
      "to": null,
      "stance": "ally",
      "cue": "RACHAEL",
      "quote": "You use your equipment, don't you?",
      "block": 56
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p5",
      "to": null,
      "stance": "neu",
      "cue": "DECKARD",
      "quote": "So?",
      "block": 57
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p6",
      "to": null,
      "stance": "ally",
      "cue": "RACHAEL",
      "quote": "So, I'm a piece of equipment.\n                  Use me.",
      "block": 58
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p5",
      "to": null,
      "stance": "neu",
      "cue": "DECKARD",
      "quote": "That's okay, I'll get it...",
      "block": 59
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p6",
      "to": null,
      "stance": "neu",
      "cue": "RACHAEL",
      "quote": "Do I make you nervous?",
      "block": 60
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p5",
      "to": null,
      "stance": "neu",
      "cue": "DECKARD",
      "quote": "Yeah.",
      "block": 61
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p6",
      "to": null,
      "stance": "neu",
      "cue": "RACHAEL",
      "quote": "It's strange to suddenly realize\n                  that what you thought was your\n                  life is actually someone else's\n                  fabrication.",
      "block": 62
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p5",
      "to": null,
      "stance": "neu",
      "cue": "DECKARD",
      "quote": "I can imagine.",
      "block": 63
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p6",
      "to": null,
      "stance": "neu",
      "cue": "RACHAEL",
      "quote": "Can you?  I couldn't.",
      "block": 64
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p6",
      "to": null,
      "stance": "neu",
      "cue": "RACHAEL",
      "quote": "A part of me is glad.  I think I\n                  feel more.  I don't like who I was\n                  before.",
      "block": 65
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p5",
      "to": null,
      "stance": "neu",
      "cue": "DECKARD",
      "quote": "So why do you think they were\n                  after their records.",
      "block": 66
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p6",
      "to": null,
      "stance": "neu",
      "cue": "RACHAEL",
      "quote": "They probably want to find out\n                  when they were made.",
      "block": 67
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p5",
      "to": null,
      "stance": "neu",
      "cue": "DECKARD",
      "quote": "Right.",
      "block": 68
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p6",
      "to": null,
      "stance": "neu",
      "cue": "RACHAEL",
      "quote": "I guess the date of your birth is\n                  important if you know you're not\n                  made to last.",
      "block": 69
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p6",
      "to": null,
      "stance": "ally",
      "cue": "RACHAEL",
      "quote": "That's my number.  If you need me.",
      "block": 70
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p6",
      "to": null,
      "stance": "opp",
      "cue": "RACHAEL",
      "quote": "You better get better locks --\n                  if you want to keep me out.",
      "block": 71
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p6",
      "to": null,
      "stance": "ally",
      "cue": "RACHAEL",
      "quote": "Good night.",
      "block": 72
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p5",
      "to": null,
      "stance": "ally",
      "cue": "DECKARD",
      "quote": "Night.",
      "block": 73
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p5",
      "to": null,
      "stance": "neu",
      "cue": "DECKARD (V.O.)",
      "quote": "The possibilities were infinite.\n                  They could change their appearances\n                  but not their future.\n                  Like she said, it was short.\n                  Longevity is what they were after.\n                  The garbage man even wanted a past.\n                  Poor fuck.  I'd check it out but\n                  I knew she was right.  The market\n                  worked on turn-over.  Built-in\n                  obsolescence was the name of the\n                  game.  That meant her too.  It\n                  was something I didn't want to",
      "block": 74
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p5",
      "to": null,
      "stance": "neu",
      "cue": "DECKARD",
      "quote": "You'd be surprised what a guy'll\n                  go through to get a glimpse of a\n                  beautiful body.",
      "block": 75
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p7",
      "to": "p5",
      "stance": "ally",
      "cue": "SALOME",
      "quote": "I bet I would.",
      "block": 76
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p5",
      "to": "p7",
      "stance": "neu",
      "cue": "DECKARD",
      "quote": "Little dirty holes the bastards\n                  drill in the wall so they can\n                  watch a lady undress.",
      "block": 77
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p7",
      "to": "p5",
      "stance": "neu",
      "cue": "SALOME",
      "quote": "And what if somebody did try to\n                  'exploit' me?  Who do I go to?",
      "block": 78
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p5",
      "to": "p7",
      "stance": "ally",
      "cue": "DECKARD",
      "quote": "Me.",
      "block": 79
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p7",
      "to": "p5",
      "stance": "neu",
      "cue": "SALOME",
      "quote": "And who do I go to about you?",
      "block": 80
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p5",
      "to": null,
      "stance": "neu",
      "cue": "DECKARD",
      "quote": "Hmmmmm?",
      "block": 81
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p8",
      "to": null,
      "stance": "neu",
      "cue": "ZHORA",
      "quote": "You ever get the feeling things\n                  aren't the way they seem?",
      "block": 82
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p5",
      "to": "p8",
      "stance": "opp",
      "cue": "DECKARD",
      "quote": "Stop or you're dead!",
      "block": 83
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p9",
      "to": "p5",
      "stance": "opp",
      "cue": "COP",
      "quote": "Drop it!",
      "block": 84
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p10",
      "to": "p5",
      "stance": "opp",
      "cue": "SERGEANT",
      "quote": "On your belly!",
      "block": 85
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p5",
      "to": "p10",
      "stance": "neu",
      "cue": "DECKARD",
      "quote": "Listen, Sergeant...",
      "block": 86
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p11",
      "to": null,
      "stance": "neu",
      "cue": null,
      "quote": "Sorry, I am not in at the moment,",
      "block": 87
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p11",
      "to": null,
      "stance": "neu",
      "cue": null,
      "quote": "but if you'll leave your name and",
      "block": 88
    },
    {
      "speaker": "p11",
      "to": null,
